<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>{{ experiment_name }} — promptdelta report</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;700&family=Newsreader:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --paper: #EDEEF0;
    --panel: #F6F7F8;
    --ink: #1B1D22;
    --muted: #6B7078;
    --rule: #C9CCD1;
    --positive: #1F6F6B;
    --positive-soft: #DCEBE9;
    --negative: #B5502D;
    --negative-soft: #F3E1D8;
    --highlight: #C98A2C;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 56px 28px 96px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 34px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .subtitle { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 36px; max-width: 60ch; }
  .hero {
    display: flex;
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: flex-end;
    padding: 28px 0 36px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-bottom: 36px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .hero-stat .num {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 56px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--highlight);
  }
  .hero-stat .label {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 8px;
    max-width: 26ch;
  }
  .meta-line {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  section { margin-bottom: 52px; }
  h2 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }
  .section-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 20px; max-width: 68ch; }
  .chart-panel {
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 24px 20px 8px;
  }
  .legend {
    display: flex;
    gap: 22px;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .legend span.dot { display: inline-block; width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 6px; }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  th, td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 9px 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  th {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; }
  .pill {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 100px;
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .pill.pos { background: var(--positive-soft); color: var(--positive); }
  .pill.neg { background: var(--negative-soft); color: var(--negative); }
  .task-block { margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .task-block h3 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 2px;
  }
  .task-desc { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin: 0 0 12px; max-width: 68ch; }
  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-top: 60px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
  }
  footer p { max-width: 72ch; }
  a { color: var(--ink); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <p class="eyebrow">promptdelta report</p>
  <h1>{{ experiment_name }}</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Same task content, same models, different envelopes. This report compares
    <strong>{{ baseline_condition }}</strong> against <strong>{{ compare_condition }}</strong> prompts
    across {{ n_models }} model{{ 's' if n_models != 1 else '' }} and {{ n_tasks }} task{{ 's' if n_tasks != 1 else '' }}.</p>

  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-stat">
      <div class="num">{{ headline_delta }}</div>
      <div class="label">avg. score change,<br>{{ baseline_condition }} → {{ compare_condition }}<br>(scale 0–1, averaged across all models &amp; tasks)</div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="meta-line">runs per cell: {{ runs_per_cell }} · temperature: {{ temperature }}</div>
      <div class="meta-line">conditions compared: {{ conditions|join(', ') }}</div>
      <div class="meta-line">generated {{ generated_at }}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>The gap, per model</h2>
    <p class="section-note">Each row is one model, averaged across all tasks. The hollow dot is the
      {{ baseline_condition }}-prompt score; the filled dot is the {{ compare_condition }}-prompt score.
      A long teal line means engineering the prompt mattered a lot for that model — a short or reversed
      line means it barely moved the needle.</p>
    <div class="chart-panel">
      <div class="legend">
        <span><span class="dot" style="background:var(--muted); opacity:0.5;"></span>{{ baseline_condition }}</span>
        <span><span class="dot" style="background:var(--positive);"></span>{{ compare_condition }} (improved)</span>
        <span><span class="dot" style="background:var(--negative);"></span>{{ compare_condition }} (no change / worse)</span>
      </div>
      {{ dumbbell_svg | safe }}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Per-task breakdown</h2>
    <p class="section-note">Mean score (0–1) and format-compliance rate per condition, for each task
      and model. Format compliance is checked independently of correctness — e.g. "did it output valid
      JSON", not "was the JSON right".</p>
    {% for task in task_blocks %}
    <div class="task-block">
      <h3>{{ task.id }}</h3>
      <p class="task-desc">{{ task.description }}</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Model</th>
            {% for c in conditions %}<th class="num">{{ c }} score</th>{% endfor %}
            {% for c in conditions %}<th class="num">{{ c }} format ok</th>{% endfor %}
            <th class="num">n / cell</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in task.rows %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ row.model_label }}</td>
            {% for c in conditions %}<td class="num">{{ row.scores.get(c, '—') }}</td>{% endfor %}
            {% for c in conditions %}<td class="num">{{ row.format_rates.get(c, '—') }}</td>{% endfor %}
            <td class="num">{{ row.n }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p>Read this with appropriate skepticism: small sample sizes per cell produce noisy means,
      LLM-judge scoring (used for subjective tasks) has its own biases toward longer or more
      confident-sounding answers, and envelope wording choices are subjective by construction.
      Treat this as a starting point for your own investigation, not a final verdict.</p>
    <p>Generated by <a href="https://github.com/">promptdelta</a>.</p>
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
